{"title":"Career Roadmap · Tribal Welfare Officer","role":"Tribal Welfare Officer","summary":"A Tribal Welfare Officer works on the planning, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation of programmes intended to improve the education, livelihoods, health, social development, rights, and economic opportunities of tribal communities. The role combines social sciences, public administration, fieldwork, community engagement, government schemes, data analysis, and programme management.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Tribal Studies / Regional Studies / Area Studies"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"Exact government post names, recruitment routes, eligibility, age limits, and departmental structures vary by state and recruitment notification. For government employment, always verify the current official notification."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Approx. Timeline","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Tribal studies + sociology + Indian polity + communication"}],[{"text":"Field Skills"},{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Community development + surveys + GIS + data"}],[{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Welfare policy + programme management + research"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Field/Programme/Community Development roles"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"3–6 years"},{"text":"Welfare Officer / Programme Officer"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"7–12 years"},{"text":"Senior/District Programme Officer"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"12–20 years"},{"text":"State/Regional Programme Leadership"}],[{"text":"Long-term"},{"text":"20+ years"},{"text":"Policy, administration, development leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Tribal & Social Science Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a s